Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code contains only the diagnosis module; BERT4Rec’s architecture 
and final sequence readout are not shown. Diagnosis accesses real-item 
embeddings through `view.item_emb.weight`, excluding padding and reserved mask 
tokens using `view.model.itemnum`. It obtains per-position sequence features 
through `view.log2feats(sequence)` and scores candidates through 
`view.predict_score(features, items)`. It does not explicitly select a final 
user representation or verify appended-mask inference.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the compatibility view and its 
`meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`; only metadata is subsequently 
consulted. The margin probe switches the view to evaluation mode and runs 
without gradients.

Up to ten loader batches supply `(None, sequence, positive, negative)`, with 
tensors shaped `B × L`. Sequences become NumPy arrays before feature extraction.
Positive and negative IDs are stacked into `B × L × 2` candidate tensors. 
Positions with positive ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings with seed 42,
normalizes them, averages off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result 
to `[0,1]`. Higher values indicate greater directional alignment; approximately 
0.5 corresponds to zero mean cosine similarity.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Computes positive score minus negative score
at valid positions. Higher mean and 10th-percentile margins suggest stronger 
separation. Lower negative-beats-positive and margin-below-0.5 rates are 
preferable.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts category occurrences separately for positive 
and negative items in low-margin and incorrectly ranked positions, retaining the
top 20 categories. These are raw counts, not frequency-normalized error rates.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, masking perturbations, ablations, or sensitivity tests 
are performed. Embedding subsampling and loader-provided negative candidates are
the only sampling involved.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering 
collapse, four margin statistics, and category breakdowns. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both sections and requests a separate JSON
interpretation with status, findings, implications, and evidence.

These are training-batch diagnostics, not validation HR@10. Masked-target 
correctness depends on the external loader and view. Category metadata is 
unavailable in this task, so category lists should remain empty. Empty 
valid-position samples produce zero margin statistics, which can misleadingly 
resemble healthy error rates.

