Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code diagnoses a BERT4Rec model through a compatibility view; the 
backbone implementation is not included. It reads real-item embeddings from 
`view.item_emb.weight[1:itemnum+1]`, excluding padding and the reserved mask 
token. Sequence representations come from `view.log2feats(sequence)` and are 
scored through `view.predict_score(features, items)`.

The probe uses features at every valid target position, rather than explicitly 
computing a final user representation. Correct masked-target handling and 
final-nonpadding readout must therefore be implemented by the underlying 
model/view; this file does not verify them.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the view and its `meta_data`, 
`review_data`, and `user_train`. Reviews and histories are retained but not 
directly analyzed. The view exposes the actual network as `view.model`.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` examines up to ten batches shaped `(None, 
sequence, positive, negative)`, with sequence and target tensors of shape B × L.
It switches to evaluation mode, disables gradients, computes sequence features, 
and scores paired positive/negative items at each position. Positions with 
positive ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings using seed 42, 
normalizes them, averages off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result 
to [0,1]. Higher values indicate stronger directional alignment; approximately 
0.5 indicates near-zero average cosine similarity.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Computes positive logit minus negative logit. 
Higher mean and 10th-percentile margins suggest clearer separation. Lower 
negative-beats-positive and margin-below-0.5 rates are preferable.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts positive and negative item categories among 
weak-margin and incorrectly ranked positions, retaining the top 20 categories. 
Category metadata is unavailable in this task, so these lists should be empty; 
counts alone do not measure normalized category difficulty.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, shuffle, ablation, gradient analysis, or SVD is 
performed. Random embedding subsampling and sampled-negative comparisons are the
only sampling-based checks.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The returned dictionary contains `metrics` and matching `metric_definitions`. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis)` embeds both into instructions for 
a separate JSON interpretation containing status, findings, implications, and 
evidence.

These training-batch diagnostics do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog 
ranking quality, sequence sensitivity, or target leakage. Empty valid-target 
batches produce zero margin metrics, which can misleadingly resemble healthy 
error rates.

