Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The supplied code exposes diagnosis logic, not the BERT4Rec implementation. It 
inspects item embeddings and sequence-position features through a model view. 
`log2feats(sequence)` supplies features; `predict_score(features, items)` scores
positive and negative candidates at each position. Final user readout, 
appended-mask inference, and correct final-nonpadding indexing cannot be 
verified from this file.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the supplied view as `self.model` and 
accesses `item_emb`, the underlying model’s `itemnum`, `meta_data`, 
`review_data`, and `user_train`. Histories and reviews are stored but unused by 
these probes.

The loader yields `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors shaped B ×
L. Sequence inputs go through `log2feats`; stacked candidates have shape B × L ×
2. Positions with positive ID zero are excluded. Margin evaluation uses 
evaluation mode and disables gradients.

# Probes & Metrics
- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings using seed 42, 
excluding padding and reserved mask tokens. It normalizes embeddings, averages 
off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result to [0,1]. Higher values 
indicate stronger directional alignment; approximately 0.5 corresponds to mean 
cosine zero, rather than necessarily unhealthy collapse.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Across at most ten batches, computes 
positive score minus negative score. Higher mean and tenth-percentile margins 
indicate stronger separation. Lower negative-beats-positive and margin-below-0.5
rates are preferable.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts positive and negative item categories in 
low-margin and incorrectly ranked cases, reporting the top twenty. Categories 
are unavailable in this benchmark, so these lists provide no supported 
category-level evidence.

# Perturbation & Tests
No sequence perturbations, shuffling, masking interventions, or sensitivity 
comparisons are performed. Candidate negatives come directly from the loader; 
diagnosis does not generate them.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, containing the 
collapse score, four margin statistics, and category breakdown. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both dictionaries into instructions 
requesting JSON with `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and 
`evidence`; it does not itself produce that interpretation.

Results depend on loader sampling, correct masked-target alignment, and score 
scale. Empty margin samples return zeros. Probes do not measure validation 
HR@10, full-catalog ranking, temporal sensitivity, gradients, or simulator 
traits, and cannot verify training or inference correctness.

