Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe expects BERT4Rec: scaled item embeddings plus absolute position 
embeddings, dropout, a bidirectional Transformer with PAD keys masked, and final
normalization. PAD=0; MASK=itemnum+1. Serving retains the latest maxlen−1 
interactions and appends MASK. Its final-slot feature represents the sequence 
for scoring; no count−1 readout is used.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
alongside `item_emb`, `log2feats(sequence)`, `predict_score(features, items)`, 
training histories, and dataset routing. The loader supplies `(None, sequence, 
positive, negative)` with B×L tensors. `run_full_diagnosis` runs in evaluation 
mode without gradients, then restores model mode and random-generator states.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** Maps mean pairwise cosine among up to 2,048 seeded 
real-item embeddings to [0,1], excluding PAD/MASK. Higher values indicate 
alignment; 0.5 means approximately zero mean cosine, not demonstrated 
representation quality.
- **Sampler and margins:** Checks reserved tokens, tensor shapes, real target 
IDs, and MASK replacement at every supervised position. Across at most ten 
batches, reports positive-minus-negative mean, tenth percentile, negative-win 
rate, and margins below 0.5. Larger margins and fewer negative wins indicate 
stronger in-sample pair separation.
- **Serving parity:** Reloads the exported category checkpoint and requires 
exact state-tensor identity. Compares explicit encoder, ModelView, internal 
scoring, exported prediction, and batched versus individual results. Passing 
requires finite, tolerance-matched scores, identical rankings, and 
short/full/truncated/batched coverage.

# Perturbation & Tests

Sensitivity runs only after sampler and parity checks pass. Up to 64 seeded 
training users contribute one eligible prefix endpoint, with a previously unseen
target and 99 unique prefix-excluded negatives.

Paired variants delete equally many recent or older visible items into PAD 
holes, preserving positions, or swap the last two items. Fixed candidates 
support target-score/rank, reciprocal-rank, hit@10 changes, top-10 overlap, and 
ranking agreement. These reveal history sensitivity; greater sensitivity is not 
inherently better. Summaries include 500 paired-user bootstrap intervals.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

Returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`: status, embedding/margin 
measurements, sampler checks, prefix counts, parity, gated sensitivity, and 
elapsed time. Sensitivity includes per-category summaries and individual 
outcomes; four-category macro results remain unavailable.

Null means unavailable. These are training-prefix diagnostics, not host 
validation quality. They cannot establish sampler provenance, uniform training 
negatives, seed robustness, external-label invariance, unavailable metadata, or 
simulator traits.

