Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe accesses item embeddings and sequence features through a 
model-compatible view; `view.model` is the actual trained network. Item 
embeddings support the collapse check, while `log2feats(sequence)` and 
`predict_score(features, items)` support ranking checks.

The supplied code does not include the BERT4Rec backbone or predictor, so it 
cannot establish how sequence representations are computed or verify 
final-nonpadding readout and appended-mask inference. The margin probe uses 
features at each valid target position rather than explicitly selecting a final 
user representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the view, device, `meta_data`, 
`review_data`, and `user_train`; the latter two are unused by these probes. 
`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` performs both checks.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors shaped 
`B × L`. Sequences pass through `log2feats`; stacked positive/negative IDs are 
scored together. Positions with positive ID zero are excluded. Ranking checks 
run in evaluation mode without gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`:** Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings using seed
42, excluding padding and reserved mask tokens. It normalizes vectors, averages 
off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result using `(mean_cosine + 1) /
2`. Higher values suggest directional collapse; approximately orthogonal 
embeddings score 0.5.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`:** Mean and lower-tail 
positive-minus-negative logits across valid positions in at most ten batches. 
Larger margins indicate stronger sampled separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`:** Fraction with margin below zero; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`:** Fraction with margin below 0.5; lower 
indicates fewer weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`:** Counts positive and negative item 
categories in weak-margin and wrong-rank cases, retaining the top 20 category 
counts per group.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, masking intervention, ablation, or sensitivity test is 
implemented. Sampling embeddings and comparing supplied negatives are the only 
sampling-based checks.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The raw result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis)` embeds both into a prompt 
requesting JSON with `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and 
`evidence`; it does not itself generate that interpretation.

These are training-sample diagnostics, not validation HR@10 or generalization 
measurements. Category metadata is unavailable in this task, so category lists 
should be empty. Empty margin samples produce zeros, which can misleadingly 
appear healthy. The probes do not verify target leakage, inference consistency, 
representation rank, or recommendation diversity.

