Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The diagnosis assumes two-layer, pre-norm BERT4Rec. Item embeddings, scaled by 
√hidden size, combine with absolute position embeddings before dropout, 
bidirectional Transformer encoding, and final normalization. PAD positions are 
excluded from attention keys. Serving retains the latest maxlen−1 history items 
and appends reserved MASK; its final-slot representation scores candidates 
through ModelView.predict_score.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

DiagnosisProbe(view, device) accesses the actual network through view.model, 
plus item_emb, log2feats, predict_score, and public user_train histories. The 
loader supplies (None, sequence, positive, negative), with B×L tensors. 
Metadata/review interfaces are retained, but unavailable attributes are not 
inferred.

Before sensitivity testing, the probe reloads the exported category checkpoint, 
verifies exact state-tensor identity, and compares explicit encoding, ModelView,
internal scoring, exported prediction, and batched scoring. Short, full-length, 
and truncated histories must pass score tolerances and exact ordered-ranking 
agreement.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** Maps mean off-diagonal cosine among up to 2,048 
real-item embeddings to [0,1]. Higher values indicate stronger alignment; 0.5 
means approximately zero average cosine, without establishing representation 
quality.
- **Masked-target separation:** Checks reserved tokens, shapes, real-item IDs, 
and all-MASK supervision across at most ten batches. Reports mean/p10 
positive-minus-negative margins and negative-wins/small-margin rates. Larger 
margins and fewer negative wins indicate better sampled training-pair 
separation.
- **History sensitivity:** Samples up to 64 training users, one eligible prefix 
endpoint each, with its target and 99 fixed unique negatives. Reports paired 
score, rank, reciprocal-rank, hit@10 changes, and ranking agreement, with 500 
bootstrap intervals.

# Perturbation & Tests

Sensitivity deletes equal numbers of recent or older items into PAD holes, 
preserving absolute positions, or swaps the last two items. Changes reveal 
dependence on history content/order, without establishing desirable behavior.

A gated, approximately 30-second residual-patching pilot corrupts the latest 
item using frequency/recency-matched donors. Hooks patch input residuals or 
first-layer outputs. Exploration selects sites/signs; disjoint confirmation 
users test effects. Identity, structural-zero, MASK-restoration, norm-matched 
random, and unrelated-history controls accompany margin/ranking measurements.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

run_full_diagnosis returns metrics and metric_definitions, including status, 
counts, sampler_contract, serving_parity, history_sensitivity, 
residual_patching, and elapsed time. Interpretation requests status, 
core_findings, key_implications, and evidence.

Failed/unavailable gates withhold sensitivity. Null means unavailable. Results 
are training-prefix diagnostics, not host validation; four-category macro 
results and global Holm adjustment require aggregation. Training trajectories, 
semantic donor compatibility, hidden labels, and unavailable user/item traits 
remain unassessed.

