Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probes target masked BERT4Rec through a ModelView wrapper; backbone 
implementation is not supplied. Relevant hooks are `item_emb`, 
`log2feats(sequence)`, and `predict_score(features, items)`. For user geometry, 
histories are truncated, left-padded, and appended with the reserved MASK token.
The user representation is the feature at the maximum nonpadding index—the 
appended MASK position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
plus training histories and metadata interfaces. It discovers `sample_batch` 
from the network’s defining module. The loader supplies `(None, sequence, 
positive, negative)` batches with matching B × L tensors. Probes validate IDs, 
shapes, and finite supervised margins, run feature extraction in evaluation 
mode, and restore the prior mode.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Directional alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings with seed 
42, averages off-diagonal pairwise cosine similarity, and maps it to [0,1]. 
Higher values indicate stronger alignment; they do not establish collapse.
- **Representation geometry:** Samples up to 256 items and users. Reports raw 
mean norm, centered variance, centered singular values, and RankMe effective 
rank. Low variance or rank can suggest restricted representations; norms alone 
are not health judgments.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Across up to ten batches, scores supplied 
positive/negative pairs at valid positions. Reports mean margin, lower-tail p10,
negative-win rate, and margin-below-0.5 rate. Larger margins and lower failure 
rates generally indicate clearer separation.
- **Coverage and allocation:** Counts valid targets, terminal targets, observed 
input types, and empty batches. Exact corruption-branch counts require matching 
sampler bookkeeping. Optional training allocation counters are read from the 
model.

# Perturbation & Tests

The probes do not independently shuffle, ablate, or corrupt histories. They 
inspect loader-supplied corruptions and construct appended-MASK inputs for 
geometry. These checks characterize training supervision and inference-style 
representations, rather than controlled sensitivity to perturbations.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering 
alignment, geometry, allocation, margins, and coverage breakdowns. Unavailable 
measurements use null; category lists remain empty because item categories are 
unavailable.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds measured values and definitions, 
requesting JSON with `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and 
`evidence`. No interpretation is executed here. These probes do not measure host
validation HR@10, recommendation diversity, causal behavior, or gradient 
contributions.

