Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe observes one fitted BERT4Rec category model through `ModelView`; model
implementation details are not supplied. Relevant hooks are `item_emb`, 
`log2feats(sequence)` and `predict_score(features, items)`. Prefix inference 
uses left-padded histories ending in a reserved MASK. The user representation is
the feature at the greatest nonpadding position—the appended MASK—never 
`count-1`.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
plus training histories and optional aligned timestamps. Metadata references are
retained, but item categories and reviews are unavailable.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with aligned `B × L` 
tensors. Feature and scoring calls prefer network methods, falling back to view 
methods. Diagnosis runs in evaluation mode without gradients, restoring module 
modes and captured RNG states afterward; iterator progress and worker-local RNGs
cannot be restored.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding similarity:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings, excluding 
PAD/MASK. Mean off-diagonal cosine is mapped to `[0,1]`; higher values indicate 
greater angular similarity, not necessarily poor recommendation diversity. Fewer
than two embeddings yields null.
- **Supervised separation:** Reads at most ten batches and scores only 
supervised MASK positions with valid positive/negative IDs. Reports mean margin,
tenth-percentile margin, negative-beats-positive rate and margin-below-0.5 rate.
Larger margins and lower failure rates indicate stronger sampled training 
separation. Audits count excluded positions; category lists remain empty.
- **Prefix dependence:** Samples up to 200 training users, treating the final 
training event as target. Scores that target against 99 fixed unique negatives. 
Reports rank, descriptive HR@10, raw/standardized margins and top-10 overlap.

# Perturbation & Tests

Frozen prefixes undergo identity copying, compact deletion of recent/oldest 
events, ten random deletions and ten recent-order permutations. Readout remains 
at MASK. Identity scores must reproduce within tolerance.

Edited-minus-baseline effects are averaged within user, then across users, with 
exploratory paired-user bootstrap intervals. Reports include no-ops, effective 
edits, strata and optional timestamp inversions. Positive HR/margin deltas 
indicate improvement; positive rank deltas indicate degradation. Sensitivity 
alone establishes neither usefulness nor causality.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering 
embedding similarity, supervised margins/audits and nested 
`recent_history_probe` results. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` requests a 
grounded JSON interpretation with status, findings, implications and evidence.

Prefix results are in-sample diagnostics, not host validation performance. 
Held-out usefulness, four-category macro effects, position-preserving deletion, 
release availability and simulator traits remain unmeasured. Missing evidence 
must remain explicit.

