is underspecified: frequency-bin boundaries, zero-count handling, donor sampling
probabilities, replacement uniqueness, bootstrap repetitions and tie-breaking 
rules are missing.', 'Donors may overlap fixed negative candidates, introducing 
candidate items into the input. Reusing one donor across replaced positions can 
also create artificial repetition. Both need explicit policies and reported 
counts.', 'Preserving positions removes compaction effects, but 
recent-versus-older differences still combine position, original-item identity, 
repetition and semantic coherence. Popularity matching alone cannot establish a 
pure recency mechanism.', 'Discarding unmatched replicates changes the analyzed 
population. Report donor support and exclusion rates by category and stratum, 
and define aggregation when users have different numbers of successful 
replicates.', 'The report lacks a primary estimand, explicit contrast signs and 
a decision rule connecting diagnostic findings to a subsequent host-validation 
experiment. Training sensitivity alone cannot establish underused useful 
history.', 'Originality 4 is reasonable for an integration contribution. 
Potential 7 is provisional without observed effects or validation association; 
difficulty 3 understates matching, reproducibility and loader-state risks. The 
cited 21.97% error rate belongs to one supplied diagnostic run and should not 
