Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe inspects the actual BERT4Rec module through `view.model`. Relevant 
hooks are catalog embeddings (`view.item_emb.weight`), sequence encoding 
(`model.log2feats`), and candidate scoring (`model.predict_score`). The encoder 
produces position-level features; diagnosis selects supervised MASK positions 
rather than pooling a final user representation. The supplied file does not show
the encoder internals or appended-mask inference implementation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` retains the model, metadata, review data, and 
training histories. The latter three are not used by the active metrics. 
Training batches provide `(None, sequence, positive, negative)`, with matching B
× L tensors.

Valid measurements require a MASK input position, valid catalog 
positive/negative IDs, and distinct positive and negative items. Labels enter 
candidate scoring only; they are never inserted into encoder inputs. Margin 
measurement temporarily switches the model to evaluation mode, disables 
gradients, and restores its previous mode.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse score:** Samples up to 2,048 catalog embeddings using 
seed 42, excludes PAD/MASK, normalizes vectors, and maps mean pairwise 
off-diagonal cosine to `(cosine + 1) / 2`. Higher values indicate greater 
directional similarity; 0.5 means mean cosine zero. This alone does not 
establish representation health or recommendation diversity.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Across at most ten batches, computes positive 
logit minus one diagnostic negative logit at each valid MASK position. Reports 
mean, nearest-rank 10th percentile, fraction below zero, and fraction below 0.5.
Larger margins and lower failure rates generally indicate stronger 
discrimination, although the 0.5 threshold depends on score scale.

# Perturbation & Tests

No extra masking, shuffling, sequence perturbation, or sensitivity comparison is
performed. Existing masked training inputs are scored directly. Shape mismatches
and nonfinite measured margins raise errors.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Metrics include
`embedding_collapse_score`, four `pos_neg_*` margin statistics, and 
`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`, containing measured-position counts, 
threshold, and low/wrong-margin counts.

Insufficient observations produce null metrics. Category lists remain empty 
because annotations are unavailable. These probes do not measure host HR@10, 
full-catalog ranking, sequence sensitivity, recommendation diversity, reviews, 
ownership, or simulator traits.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds measured values and definitions into a 
prompt requesting JSON with `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and 
`evidence`; it does not itself generate that interpretation.

