Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probes target masked BERT4Rec through a ModelView wrapper; the backbone 
implementation is not included. Relevant interfaces are `item_emb`, 
`log2feats(sequence)`, and `predict_score(features, items)`. For user geometry, 
histories are left-padded, truncated to reserve space for an appended MASK, and 
encoded. The final representation is selected at the maximum nonpadding 
index—the appended MASK position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
plus training histories and metadata interfaces. It locates `sample_batch` in 
the network’s defining module to inspect optional corruption bookkeeping.

The margin probe consumes at most ten `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` 
batches with matching B × L shapes. It validates IDs and scoring shapes, obtains
per-position features, and scores positive/negative pairs as B × L × 2 logits. 
Feature probes use evaluation mode and restore the prior mode.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Directional alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings, excluding
padding/MASK. Mean off-diagonal cosine is mapped to [0,1]. Higher values 
indicate stronger alignment, but do not establish collapse.
- **Representation geometry:** Separately samples up to 256 items and users. 
Reports raw norms, centered variance, centered singular values, and RankMe 
effective rank. Small variance or low rank can suggest limited representation 
variation; no universal healthy thresholds are defined.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Reports mean, tenth percentile, negative-wins 
rate, and fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and lower error/small-margin rates 
indicate stronger sampled training separation.
- **Coverage/allocation:** Counts valid targets, terminal supervision, observed 
input types, and matched corruption branches. Optional network counters describe
training allocation, not gradient shares or validation quality.

# Perturbation & Tests

No independent sequence-shuffling, deletion, or sensitivity experiment is 
performed. The probe observes sampler-produced MASK/random/unchanged corruption,
identifying branches only when bookkeeping exactly matches the batch. 
Appended-MASK histories test representation geometry under the inference input 
convention.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Category 
breakdowns remain empty because item categories are unavailable; unsupported 
measurements return null. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds these outputs 
and requests a grounded JSON interpretation with status, findings, implications,
and evidence.

These sampled training probes do not measure host validation HR@10, full-catalog
ranking quality, recommendation diversity, causal sensitivity, or 
generalization.

