Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probes assume a two-layer, pre-norm BERT4Rec encoder: scaled item embeddings
plus absolute position embeddings, dropout, bidirectional attention with PAD-key
masking, and final normalization. Serving left-pads histories, retains at most 
`maxlen−1` items, and appends reserved MASK. Candidate logits use the final MASK
representation through `view.predict_score`; deletion never moves the readout.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
plus `item_emb`, `log2feats`, `predict_score`, training histories, metadata, and
dataset routing. The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with
matching B×L tensors.

Before sensitivity analysis, sampler checks verify reserved tokens, MASK at 
supervised positions, and valid distinct positive/negative IDs. Serving parity 
reloads the current category’s exported checkpoint, verifies exact state-tensor 
identity, and compares explicit encoder, ModelView, internal scoring, exported 
prediction, and batched outputs. Short, full-length, and truncated histories 
must pass score tolerances and identical ranking checks.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** Maps mean off-diagonal cosine among up to 2,048 
sampled real-item embeddings into [0,1]. Larger values indicate alignment; 0.5 
indicates approximately zero mean cosine, without proving representation 
quality.
- **Sampled-pair separation:** Across at most ten loader batches, reports 
mean/p10 positive-minus-negative margins, negative-win rate, and margins below 
0.5. Larger margins and fewer negative wins indicate stronger in-sample 
separation.
- **History sensitivity:** Samples up to 64 training users and one eligible 
endpoint each, using a fixed target plus 99 unique prefix-excluded negatives. 
Reports paired score, rank, reciprocal-rank, hit@10, overlap, and 
ranking-agreement changes with bootstrap intervals. Sensitivity alone is neither
good nor bad.

# Perturbation & Tests

History variants delete equally many recent or older items into PAD holes, 
preserving positions, or swap the final two items.

A nominally 30-second residual-patching pilot corrupts the latest item using 
frequency/recency-matched donors, then restores or disrupts residuals before 
either attention layer. Exploration selects sites/signs; disjoint confirmation 
users support sign tests. Identity, final-history structural-zero, 
MASK-restoration, norm-matched random, and unrelated-history controls accompany 
effects.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`: status, 
embedding/margin statistics, sampler checks, parity, sensitivity, 
residual-patching records/summaries, counts, availability, and timing. The 
interpreter requests evidence-linked JSON findings.

These are training-prefix diagnostics, not host validation. Single-category 
views cannot establish four-category macro results or global Holm discoveries. 
Missing data remain null/unavailable; convergence, seed uncertainty, unavailable
metadata, intent, repair benefits, and recommendation-quality gains remain 
unassessed.

