Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probes expect a BERT4Rec encoder with catalog item embeddings, padding ID 0,
and reserved mask ID `itemnum + 1`. Inference retains the latest `L−1` history 
items, appends a mask, and left-pads to length L. The user representation is 
`encode_sequence(tokens)[:, -1]`; candidate scores are dot products with item 
embeddings. The backbone implementation is not supplied here.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
plus `item_emb`, `log2feats`, `predict_score`, and training histories. The 
loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` tensors of matching B×L 
shape. A temporary embedding pre-hook captures live inference tokens. Diagnosis 
runs in evaluation/inference mode and restores module modes and Python, NumPy, 
CPU, and CUDA RNG states afterward.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Integrity:** Checks reserved-mask IDs, appended-mask input construction, 
finite scores, live/reference score agreement, padding invariance, and 
incorrect-readout controls. Explicit failures gate history sensitivity; 
unavailable checks remain unknown.
- **Embedding collapse:** Computes rescaled mean pairwise cosine over up to 
2,048 catalog embeddings. Higher values indicate greater angular alignment; this
alone establishes neither quality nor diversity.
- **Masked-target margins:** Across up to ten batches, measures 
positive-minus-negative logits only at valid supervised mask positions. Reports 
mean, tenth percentile, negative-outranking rate, and margin-below-0.5 rate. 
Larger margins and lower failure rates indicate stronger training-target 
separation.
- **History sensitivity:** For up to 200 users, recovers each final training 
event from its preceding history. Reports target score, rank, HR@10, 
hardest-negative margin, intervention deltas, and top-10 overlap, with 
user-bootstrap intervals and repeat/explore, length, and popularity strata.

# Perturbation & Tests

Structural fixtures cover empty, short, full-length, and repeated histories. 
Tests perturb padding embeddings and right-context tokens, omit the appended 
mask, and use the erroneous `count−1` readout. History interventions remove or 
mask oldest/newest blocks. Three separate candidate draws remain fixed across 
interventions. Sensitivity has no universally desirable direction.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including 
integrity, collapse, margins, counts, reasons, and sensitivity summaries. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` requests an evidence-grounded JSON 
interpretation.

Training recovery is not held-out generalization or causal preference evidence. 
Actual sampler provenance, fresh-process checkpoint/predictor parity, and 
attention deletion remain uncertified. Category metadata and review attributes 
are unavailable; no four-category macro is computed.

