Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe targets masked BERT4Rec through a ModelView wrapper; the backbone 
implementation is not supplied. Relevant hooks are `item_emb`, 
`log2feats(sequence)`, and `predict_score(features, items)`. For user geometry, 
it left-pads training histories, reserves space for an appended MASK token, and 
selects its representation at the maximum nonpadding index. Margin probes score 
each supervised position’s features.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual module through `view.model`, 
plus histories and metadata through the wrapper. It discovers `sample_batch` in 
the module’s defining Python module to retrieve corruption bookkeeping.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` tensors with matching
B × L shapes. The probe validates token ranges, score shapes, and finite 
supervised margins. Feature probes use evaluation mode without gradients and 
restore the previous training mode.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Directional alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings, excluding
padding and MASK. Mean pairwise cosine is mapped to [0,1]; higher indicates 
stronger alignment, without proving collapse.
- **Representation geometry:** Separately samples up to 256 items and users. 
Reports raw norms, centered variance, centered singular values, and RankMe 
effective rank. Narrow spectra suggest limited representational variation; no 
universal healthy threshold is supplied.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Across up to ten batches, computes mean 
margin, tenth-percentile margin, negative-wins rate, and margin-below-0.5 rate. 
Larger margins and lower failure rates indicate stronger sampled training 
separation.
- **Coverage and allocation:** Counts valid targets, terminal targets, observed 
input types, and matched corruption branches. Optional runtime training counters
describe branch allocation; coefficient shares do not measure gradient shares.

# Perturbation & Tests

The geometry probe appends MASK to histories, matching inference-style readout. 
Margin probes inspect sampler-corrupted inputs and identify 
mask/random/unchanged branches only when bookkeeping matches exactly. There are 
no paired perturbation or causal sensitivity tests.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering 
alignment, geometry, training allocation, four margin summaries, and 
coverage/breakdown details. Unavailable measurements use nulls or explicit 
status text. Item-category breakdowns remain empty because categories are 
unavailable.

These training probes do not measure host validation HR@10, recommendation 
diversity, generalization, or unobserved user traits. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds the measurements and definitions into a 
prompt requesting a separate JSON interpretation with status, findings, 
implications, and evidence.

