Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe inspects item embeddings and sequence-conditioned positive/negative 
scores. Model implementation is not supplied, so representation computation 
cannot be verified. `log2feats(sequence)` supplies position-wise features; 
`predict_score(features, items)` scores candidates at each position. The probe 
does not explicitly extract a final sequence representation or verify 
final-nonpadding readout and appended-mask inference.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` receives the compatibility view, although the 
constructor names it `model`. It accesses `item_emb`, `log2feats`, 
`predict_score`, `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`; the latter two 
are stored but unused. `view.model.itemnum` identifies real item IDs.

The loader yields `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors shaped `B 
× L`. Sequences pass through `log2feats`; stacked positive/negative IDs have 
shape `B × L × 2`. Positions with positive ID zero are excluded. Margin 
evaluation uses evaluation mode and disables gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 real item embeddings using seed 
42, excludes padding/reserved tokens, normalizes vectors, and averages 
off-diagonal cosine similarities. Mapping `(mean_cosine + 1)/2` produces the 
score. Higher indicates directional similarity; approximately 0.5 corresponds to
zero average cosine, not necessarily collapse.
- **Positive/negative separation:** Across at most ten batches, computes 
`positive_logit − negative_logit`. Higher mean and tenth-percentile margins 
indicate stronger separation. Lower negative-win rates (`margin < 0`) and 
small-margin rates (`margin < 0.5`) are preferable.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts category memberships separately for positive 
and negative items in weak-margin and wrong-ranking cases, retaining the top 20 
per group. These are raw counts, not normalized error rates.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, shuffling, ablation, or sensitivity test runs. Random 
embedding sampling and supplied negative candidates are the only sampling 
components.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering 
collapse, four margin statistics, and category breakdowns. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds these in instructions requesting a 
separate JSON interpretation with status, findings, implications, and evidence.

Category metadata is unavailable in this task, so breakdown lists should be 
empty. Metrics assess sampled training positions, not validation HR@10, 
full-catalog ranking, or generalization. Missing valid positions produce zero 
margin statistics, which can misleadingly resemble healthy error rates. Correct 
masked-target construction depends on the external loader/model contract.

