Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The probes expect one BERT4Rec network per category, accessed through 
`ModelView`. Relevant hooks are `item_emb`, `encode_sequence`, 
`score_candidates`, `log2feats`, and `predict_score`. Encoder implementation is 
not supplied. Inference histories are left-padded, truncated to L−1 items, and 
followed by a reserved mask token. The final sequence representation is 
`encode_sequence(tokens)[:, -1]`; candidate scores use its dot product with item
embeddings.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` reads the actual network from `view.model` and 
public training histories from `view.user_train`. 
`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` switches to evaluation/inference mode and 
restores module modes and Python, NumPy, and Torch RNG states afterward.

Consumed records are sought on the loader, view, then network. At most four 
captured batches are replayed; the production iterator is never advanced. Margin
probes call `view.log2feats(sequence)` and `view.predict_score(features, 
stacked_items)`.

# Probes & Metrics
- **Integrity:** Checks reserved-mask IDs, observed inference tokens, finite 
scores, live score agreement, padding invariance, and incorrect-readout 
controls. Explicit failures block history sensitivity; missing checks remain 
unavailable.
- **Consumed-pipeline audit:** Reconstructs crops, event positions, masks, 
labels, and seeded negatives from histories. When captured logits exist, 
recomputes CE/BPR terms and scalar reduction. Agreement supports bounded 
consistency, not gradient correctness.
- **Embedding collapse:** Maps mean pairwise catalog-embedding cosine to [0,1]. 
Values near 1 indicate angular alignment; approximately 0.5 indicates average 
cosine near zero. Neither alone establishes recommendation quality.
- **Masked-target margins:** Reports mean, tenth percentile, 
negative-beats-positive rate, and margin-below-0.5 rate. Larger margins and 
lower error rates indicate stronger training-target separation.

# Perturbation & Tests
Structural fixtures cover empty, short, full-length, and repeated-item 
histories. Tests perturb padding embeddings and right context, omit the mask, 
and use an incorrect count−1 readout. Audit calibration injects verified 
label/mask faults with reversible restoration and clean controls.

History sensitivity uses up to 200 users’ last training events. It deletes or 
masks oldest/newest blocks, comparing scores, ranks, HR@10, margins, and top-10 
overlap against frozen candidates across three draws. Reports include bootstrap 
intervals and repeat/explore, length, and popularity strata.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
Output contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including 
`bert4rec_integrity`, `consumed_pipeline_audit`, collapse/margin statistics, and
`training_history_sensitivity`. Missing observations carry nulls, counts, and 
reasons. Training recovery is not held-out generalization; interventions do not 
establish causal preferences. Fresh-process predictor parity, complete gradient 
wiring, attention-mask inspection, and four-category macro validation remain 
uncertified. Unavailable item-category metadata leaves breakdowns empty.

